# PR Review Cycle — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## 1. Push once and open the PR
The branch is pushed **once**, when the feature is ready and green. Then:
```
gh pr create --base {{BASE_BRANCH}} --head <branch> --title "<type>: <short>" \
  --body "<what & why; the plan file; slices; how it was verified>"
PR=$(gh pr view --json number -q .number)
```

## 2. Review
1. `gh pr diff $PR` (and `gh pr diff $PR --name-only` for the scope list).
2. Spawn the **pr-reviewer** agent (and **security-reviewer** for auth, payments, user data or new endpoints) on the diff. Optional `skip-<agent>` flags skip a reviewer; name every skipped one in the summary.
3. Post the findings as ONE review with inline comments:
   ```
   gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/$PR/reviews -X POST -f event=COMMENT \
     -f body="Automated review (pr-reviewer). N findings — see inline comments." \
     -F 'comments[][path]=<file>' -F 'comments[][line]=<line>' -F 'comments[][side]=RIGHT' \
     -F 'comments[][body]=**[blocker] <title>** — <fix>'
   ```

## 3. Fix (scope and rounds)
- A fix touches only files already in the PR (`gh pr diff $PR --name-only`); a finding that needs another file is fixed only if it is in the ticket's scope, and its reply says so.
- Re-run the gate until green; verify for real; update the KB if behaviour changed.
- Commit the round's fixes, then push **once** for the round, never once per finding.
- **At most 3 rounds.** If round 3 still has blockers, stop and hand the PR to the developer with the open findings listed.

## 4. Reply and resolve
Reply on each fixed thread (`Fixed in <sha>: <what changed>`), then resolve it with the GraphQL
`resolveReviewThread` mutation. A false positive gets a reply explaining why, then is resolved. Re-read every
thread from the previous round before claiming "all addressed": silence about a finding is not a fix.

## 5. Hand off
Post a final summary comment (findings, what was fixed, what is left). Give the developer the PR URL: **they
test and merge**; there is no separate approval step and the agent never merges.
